 kit flow - shows where the work stands, from backlog to releases

   required
   --no-fetch --fresh [--text | --json | --jq] [--all | [--mine] [--others] [--owner=<login>…]]
   --stages                  prints the stages the picture draws, one per line, in order
   --me                      prints the caller's login on the primary's forge, the login --mine and
                             --others match
   backlog                   the open issues not closed by any open pull request, oldest first;
                             underway has the rest
   underway                  the open issues closed by an open pull request: who works on each, and
                             where
   incoming                  what fetching every remote brought: default-branch commits, branches
                             new and gone
   desk                      the root checkout: branch, ahead and behind, uncommitted paths
   worktrees                 every linked worktree: branch, ahead and behind, uncommitted paths
   changes                   the open pull requests, each with the issues it closes
   builds                    the runs not owned by any pull request: the default branch, tags,
                             schedules
   releases                  the releases on the forge, newest first


 kit flow
